1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,268
A parent bought the bakery's millet
laddoos, thinking they were Laddoo

2
00:00:04,268 --> 00:00:05,168
Lab's.

3
00:00:05,069 --> 00:00:06,637
Both packs looked alike.

4
00:00:06,637 --> 00:00:09,020
Plain, with a name in small letters.

5
00:00:09,570 --> 00:00:13,807
Zoya realises she has a good
product, but not yet a strong brand.

6
00:00:14,457 --> 00:00:17,332
So Dev, the designer,
takes charge of the look.

7
00:00:17,682 --> 00:00:22,590
His job: make Laddoo Lab easy to spot,
easy to remember, and hard to copy.

8
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:24,296
Nani adds one rule.

9
00:00:24,296 --> 00:00:27,499
The brand must tell the
truth about what is inside.

10
00:00:28,149 --> 00:00:29,526
So what is a brand?

11
00:00:29,826 --> 00:00:34,495
The American Marketing Association
calls it a name, term, design, symbol

12
00:00:34,495 --> 00:00:38,616
or any other feature that sets
one seller apart from the rest.

13
00:00:38,966 --> 00:00:41,693
The word comes from an
old word for burning.

14
00:00:41,693 --> 00:00:45,816
Makers burned marks onto barrels
and cattle, to show what was theirs.

15
00:00:46,166 --> 00:00:47,899
Today, a brand is a promise.

16
00:00:47,899 --> 00:00:50,782
When you see the mark, you
know what you will get.

17
00:00:51,432 --> 00:00:54,816
Let's watch Dev build the
brand, one piece at a time.

18
00:00:55,166 --> 00:00:56,435
First, the name.

19
00:00:56,435 --> 00:00:57,335
Laddoo Lab.

20
00:00:57,313 --> 00:01:00,854
Short, easy to say, and it
tells you what is inside.

21
00:01:01,204 --> 00:01:04,301
Dev tests it with Kevin
Lane Keller's six checks.

22
00:01:04,301 --> 00:01:06,932
Is it memorable, meaningful and likable?

23
00:01:07,282 --> 00:01:12,045
Can it stretch to new products, adapt
over time, and be protected by law?

24
00:01:12,045 --> 00:01:13,386
It passes all six.

25
00:01:13,736 --> 00:01:14,949
Next, the logo.

26
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:18,762
Dev draws a round laddoo, and
adds a small leaf for health.

27
00:01:19,112 --> 00:01:23,479
He removes extra lines, until it
still works at the size of a coin.

28
00:01:23,829 --> 00:01:25,196
Then, the colours.

29
00:01:25,196 --> 00:01:29,317
Navy for trust, jaggery gold for
warmth, and cream for home-made.

30
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:31,109
Then, the tagline.

31
00:01:31,109 --> 00:01:33,489
The healthy sweet for tiffin boxes.

32
00:01:33,489 --> 00:01:36,182
It says exactly where Laddoo Lab stands.

33
00:01:36,532 --> 00:01:37,914
Finally, the pack.

34
00:01:37,914 --> 00:01:42,484
Every flavour gets the same logo and
colours, with its own flavour band.

35
00:01:42,834 --> 00:01:46,765
Now, from across a shop, a parent
spots Laddoo Lab in a second.

36
00:01:47,415 --> 00:01:49,595
A product is made in a kitchen.

37
00:01:49,595 --> 00:01:51,874
A brand is made in people's minds.

38
00:01:52,574 --> 00:01:54,204
Why does a brand matter?

39
00:01:54,204 --> 00:01:55,591
It helps both sides.

40
00:01:55,941 --> 00:01:57,755
For buyers, it saves time.

41
00:01:57,755 --> 00:01:59,708
They find their favourite fast.

42
00:02:00,008 --> 00:02:01,067
It lowers risk.

43
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:03,983
They know the taste will
be the same every time.

44
00:02:04,283 --> 00:02:07,691
For sellers, it builds loyalty,
so customers come back.

45
00:02:07,991 --> 00:02:12,419
And it protects them from copies,
because the name and logo belong to them.

46
00:02:13,069 --> 00:02:15,036
Where do we see this at work today?

47
00:02:15,386 --> 00:02:16,286
Names.

48
00:02:15,974 --> 00:02:19,862
A food delivery app picks a
short name that is easy to type.

49
00:02:20,212 --> 00:02:21,112
Logos.

50
00:02:20,872 --> 00:02:24,387
A bank's logo still works
on a tiny phone screen.

51
00:02:24,737 --> 00:02:25,637
Colours.

52
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:28,927
An airline paints every plane
in the same two colours.

53
00:02:29,277 --> 00:02:30,177
Taglines.

54
00:02:30,089 --> 00:02:33,616
A phone maker repeats one
short line in every ad.

55
00:02:34,266 --> 00:02:37,019
But can a brand make a bad product good?

56
00:02:37,019 --> 00:02:37,919
No.

57
00:02:37,823 --> 00:02:38,921
The good side.

58
00:02:38,921 --> 00:02:42,614
A strong brand earns trust,
and trust brings people back.

59
00:02:42,964 --> 00:02:44,075
The hard side.

60
00:02:44,075 --> 00:02:45,649
A brand is a promise.

61
00:02:45,649 --> 00:02:48,176
Break it once, and trust falls fast.

62
00:02:48,526 --> 00:02:51,718
Dev wants a big sticker:
best laddoos in India.

63
00:02:51,718 --> 00:02:52,783
Nani says no.

64
00:02:52,783 --> 00:02:54,300
We cannot prove that.

65
00:02:54,650 --> 00:02:58,536
So the pack says only what is
true: made with ragi and jaggery.

66
00:02:58,886 --> 00:03:04,183
In India, the Trade Marks Act of 1999
protects a registered mark for ten

67
00:03:04,183 --> 00:03:07,807
years, and it can be
renewed again and again.

68
00:03:08,157 --> 00:03:09,073
The lesson?

69
00:03:09,073 --> 00:03:10,666
A brand is a promise.

70
00:03:10,666 --> 00:03:12,658
Keep it, every single time.

71
00:03:13,308 --> 00:03:14,208
Quick check.

72
00:03:14,205 --> 00:03:16,822
A name, a logo, colours and a tagline.

73
00:03:16,822 --> 00:03:18,292
What are these called?

74
00:03:20,192 --> 00:03:21,251
Brand elements!

75
00:03:21,251 --> 00:03:24,665
The parts that make a brand
easy to spot and remember.

76
00:03:25,265 --> 00:03:26,277
So, remember.

77
00:03:26,577 --> 00:03:31,324
A brand is a name, logo or symbol
that sets you apart from rivals.

78
00:03:31,674 --> 00:03:36,874
Good brand elements are memorable,
meaningful, likable, flexible and protectable.

79
00:03:37,224 --> 00:03:39,945
And a brand is a promise
that must be kept.

80
00:03:40,545 --> 00:03:45,239
Next time, we compare who Laddoo Lab
wants to be with how people see it:

81
00:03:45,239 --> 00:03:47,314
brand identity and brand image.
